  "body": "High on the ridgeline above St Heliers, 27A Auckland Road takes in spectacular views across the Hauraki Gulf. A substantial north-facing home is situated on the freehold site here, with several living spaces, manicured gardens and the beach and village a short\r\nwalk down the road.\r\n\r\nThe home has monolithic cladding, and that is the opportunity. Whether you are a family seeking a foothold in this prestigious location or a tradesperson, experienced renovator, re-cladder or buyer looking to add value, this is a chance to secure the position and bring your own\r\nexpertise and ideas. Bring your architect and builder to explore how the existing home could be renewed, or live here happily while designing a home around the elevation and views, subject to the necessary consents.\r\n\r\nThe layout spans three levels, with several living areas, three bedrooms plus a study, three bathrooms and triple garaging. A lounge and balcony on the uppermost level take in the Hauraki Gulf outlook, while the ground-floor living room opens to a courtyard surrounded by manicured gardens. There is room for family life here, with places to gather, entertain and spend time outdoors.\r\n\r\nWalk down Auckland Road to St Heliers Beach and the village for a morning swim and coffee. Kohimarama and Mission Bay extend the choice of beaches, cafes and restaurants, connected by the waterfront. Madills Farm provides sports fields, a playground and space for a weekend walk with the family. The property is zoned for St Heliers School, Glendowie College, St Ignatius Catholic School and Baradene College.\r\n\r\nSurplus to the owner's requirements and selling well below the CV of $2.225m, we strongly recommend viewing 27A Auckland Road at your earliest convenience.\r\n\r\nA building report is available to assist with your due diligence.\r\n\r\nFOUND: Freehold land, Mixed Housing Suburban zone, expansive views.",
